+## Comparing with the Go blog
+
+`make compare` fetches the same paths from the Go blog and the Worker and
+reports, path by path, whether the status, `Content-Type`, and body match.
+Start both first, each in its own terminal:
+
+```sh
+(cd ../go && go run ./examples/blog -addr localhost:8080)
+make dev PORT=8798
+make compare GO_URL=http://localhost:8080 PORT=8798
+make compare GO_URL=http://localhost:8080 PORT=8798 PATHS="/docs /posts/hello.md"
+```
+
+Without `PATHS` it compares `/`, a post, a document, `/docs/`,
+`/favicon.svg`, and a path with nothing at it. Redirects are not
+followed, and each server's own base URL in a body is replaced with
+`{BASE_URL}` before comparing, so the OGP tags do not differ by port
+alone. It exits with an error when any path differs. The CLI is a native
+executable built on `moonbitlang/async`, which does not support wasm-gc;
+`compare/cmd` builds only for native and `worker` only for wasm-gc, so
+the Worker's Wasm is unchanged.
+
